# PCPI AISTATS Mainline Guardrails

- Treat PCPI as sequential Bayesian discrimination among predictive equivalence classes of symbolic laws.
- Keep C1--C3 primary: Bayesian formulation/classes, target-correct SMC, and defensible acquisition. Motifs, LLM orchestration, and VED are extensions and must not delay or inflate C1--C3.
- Efficacy experiments must use provenance-audited real measured data (for example Airfoil, CCPP, Gas Turbine, NIST ASD, or audited VED). Never use simulated or synthetic data to support superiority or discovery claims.
- Tiny controlled fixtures are allowed only for numerical correctness (posterior, likelihood, SMC, resampling, convergence, EIG estimator). Label them `inference correctness diagnostic fixture`.
- Preserve development, validation, acquisition-pool, and untouched-heldout roles. Algorithm code must never access held-out arrays, paths, shapes, ranges, statistics, metadata, or results before the registered one-time confirmation.
- Codex changes and verifies code only. Do not launch formal experiments or consume experiment budgets; give the user exact reproducible commands to run.
- A smoke test or dry-run is allowed only when it does not constitute a formal experiment or inspect held-out data; state this clearly.
- Do not advance the paper phase when evidence misses a declared gate or paper-quality threshold. Report NO-GO and diagnose the methodological cause.
- Improve weak results through principled algorithmic changes grounded in theory and current primary literature/source code. Never hard-code answers, dataset identities, task-specific formulas, seeds, thresholds, or post-hoc regularizers chosen from evaluation/held-out outcomes.
- Do not tune against untouched-heldout or repeatedly inspect it. Freeze algorithm, dependencies, priors, likelihood, kernels, acquisition, budgets, seeds, splits, failure policy, metrics, and go/no-go conditions before one-time confirmation.
- Require matched observation and compute budgets, shared posterior engine, fixed splits/seeds, multi-seed reporting, paired uncertainty, failure accounting, and claim--code--evidence traceability.
- Call acquisition EIG only after exact-reference validation; otherwise name it honestly (for example posterior-disagreement acquisition). Call weights/posteriors Bayesian only when the implemented probabilistic target justifies it.
- Gates are sequential: exact reference -> target-correct fixed/trans-dimensional SMC -> acquisition validation -> real-data evidence -> submission evidence. Do not bypass a failed gate.
